      "title": "Aha insight",
      "body": "The problem is to count the number of islands in a 2D grid where '1' represents land and '0' represents water. We can solve this problem using Depth-First Search (DFS) algorithm. For each cell that contains '1', we perform DFS to explore all adjacent land cells and mark them as visited by changing their value to '0'. This way, we count each connected component of '1's as a separate island."
